    "head_commit_message": "feat(formation): loose and fleeing places live in the unit store\n\nSpec 35 step 1b (Decision 142). Loose entries no longer hold \"at\" and\nfleeing entries no longer hold \"offset\": both are store columns (LOOSE_AT,\nFLEE_OFFSET), with a FLAGS column whose LOOSE and FLEEING bits say whether\na unit has each entry. SquadEntries is the only place entries are given or\ntaken away, so the bits always match them. Passes over many units read the\ncolumns once; scattered reads go through SquadEntries.loose_at. The digest\nrebuilds the entries with their places, so its bytes are unchanged. The\none-mover check now covers writes to the two new place columns.\n\nPre-existing files modified beyond the OCP limit, under Decision 142's waiver.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01D25MB57Z7nmE6u7pDpd3yj",
